  "contract": [
    "All256 valid uint8 function IDs route as native:0 ADT,1 HR,2 HRV,6 SpO2,9/15 NADT, otherwise no_ver. Null output returns without writing.",
    "The ADT getter returns stable read-only identity text; pointer numeric address changes with layout and is not an identity requirement. DSP/DLCOM return the destination, qualifier returns1 and writes exactly nc without a terminator; algorithm builders return0.",
    "All512 caller-buffer bytes plus guards compared, including bytes after the terminator. All3 seed patterns and both PRIMASK values exercised. Maximum returned version text is126 bytes.",
    "Separate native ABI providers supersede portable capacity-taking symbol hints. Existing portable implementations are retained for their own API consumers."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No providers are modeled. Native string helpers and version graph execute directly; compiled C graph links the existing C memclr4/memset implementations. Source cannot execute stock. All768 admitted native instruction bytes execute.",
    "Saved integer/FP registers, SP, masks and guards preserved on normal return. Void dispatcher scratch, APSR, private stack addresses and private scratch bytes excluded; no physical hardware or concurrency proof.",
    "Stock6a020 copies the requested count as raw bytes. At its50-byte caller this overreads its terminated18-byte identity into adjacent executable instructions. It is not a bounded string copy. The C SpO2 caller uses a private text-only helper, preserving complete output and avoiding retained instruction data. The unused private scratch tail differs.",
    "Unchecked get_Spo2WRWeights_version0x6a020 is deliberately not exported, mapped or admitted as a native C provider. The separately pinned stock helper remains an analysis boundary for direct arbitrary-count callers. Do not claim this native ABI is reconstructed.",
    "Nine admitted entry points and the entire public dispatcher output are checked, not byte or instruction identity. Larger-than-uint8 IDs and invalid output pointers are outside this API corpus.",
    "The first fixture exposed the weights raw-copy contract; its initial standalone bounded-copy candidate was removed from the exported graph before admission. Only verify-final.log and the final eight compiled defects are admission evidence.",
    "No new writable state or added imports.867 prior nongenerated source/object pairs unchanged. The final tested object equals the normal878-unit build. Application imports fall61 to60; bootloader remains22.",
    "Final executable linking, startup, physical sensor operation and boot remain open. Relocatable composition is not bootable firmware."
  ],
